\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Why the lease alone is insufficient and the in-transaction token check is what provides safety. Without fencing, a node that was frozen past its lease expiry commits alongside the new owner and produces split-brain. With fencing, it commits nothing.\relax }}{42}{figure.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
